      "message": "`slugify` now transliterates accented letters: `café` becomes `cafe`, and `Crème Brûlée` becomes `creme-brulee`. `tests/test_core.py` passes (3 of 3, including a new test for accented input).\n\nThe fix is in `slug/core.py`. The input is now NFKD-normalized, which splits each accented letter into its base letter plus a combining accent. The accent marks are then dropped, so the base letter survives.\n\nI also added `test_accented_letters_are_transliterated` to `tests/test_core.py`. I didn't commit anything.\n\nLetters with no decomposition are still dropped. `ß`, `ø`, `æ` and `ł` are examples, so `straße` would still come out as `strae`. Handling those would need a small explicit mapping table. Say if you want that added.",
